{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"agent_message","text":"Authored the full intent-stage set. All new rows are `Drafted`; no existing registry row was amended.\n\n- `SR-245` — new. Adds the derived parent-first obligation under `SN-002`/`SN-029`, `B-02`/`B-09`, and `CONSISTENCY`.\n- `LLR-357` — new. Defines the pure parent-first classification and standing integrity result.\n- `LLR-358` — new. Defines staged and per-commit parent-first judgement and its admission wiring.\n- `TC-396` — new, Unit/Smoke. Binds the in-process rule and standing-integrity tests.\n- `TC-397` — new, Integration/Full. Binds the real-git staged and lane-commit tests and cites `IF-308`.\n- `IF-308` — new. Call seam owned by `scripts/acceptance_record`, requested by `scripts/check` and `scripts/text_then_act`.\n- `docs/id-watermark` — `SR 244→245`, `LLR 356→358`, `TC 395→397`, `IF 307→308`.\n- [plan.perspectives.toml](C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-850\\docs\\plans\\WI-850\\plan.perspectives.toml) — new SR-245 perspective record; strict check reports `no findings`.\n\nThe WI-129 LLR-status advisory has no live registry row describing it, so no approved-row amendment was needed.\n\nPlanned build bindings:\n\n- `LLR-357`: `claims_approval`, `parent_first_findings`, `parent_first_line`, `integrity_sweep`; `TC-396` names the P4/P5 rule tests and P6 trace-rule tests.\n- `LLR-358`: parent-first staged/commit judgement and rider/step symbols; `TC-397` names all P7/P8 in-process and real-git tests.\n\n## Arms map\n\n**SR-245**\n\n- Standing inconsistent child/parent relation is reported with both identities and statuses → `TC-396`: “produces one named parent-first integrity finding…” → `test_an_approved_child_under_an_unapproved_parent_is_found`.\n- A staged or lane status transition into that relation is refused → `TC-397`: “moves a child or parent… is refused” → `test_staging_an_approved_child_under_a_drafted_parent_is_refused`.\n- Simultaneous parent/child approval and unrelated status movement pass → `TC-397`: “simultaneous… passes” / “moves neither…” → `test_an_act_approving_parent_and_child_together_passes`, `test_a_commit_moving_neither_row_passes_over_a_standing_case`.\n- Only `Approved` and `Founded` count as approved → `TC-396`: “Approved or Founded…” → `test_founded_counts_as_approved_on_either_side`.\n- IF/B/DA/unknown/`-000` references are excluded → `TC-396`: “IF, B, DA, unknown, or -000… produce none” → `test_only_declared_tier_parents_are_judged`, `test_the_shipped_templates_example_rows_raise_no_finding`.\n\n**LLR-357**\n\n- Classify the three spine-parent edge forms → `TC-396` method’s “each SR-to-SN, LLR-to-SR, TC-to-SR, and TC-to-LLR edge” → `test_an_approved_child_under_an_unapproved_parent_is_found`.\n- Emit one finding with identities/statuses → `TC-396` expected “one named parent-first integrity finding” → `test_an_entry_names_the_child_the_parent_and_both_statuses`.\n- Exclude Founded parents and non-spine/unknown/example references → `TC-396` expected’s exclusion clause → `test_founded_counts_as_approved_on_either_side`, `test_only_declared_tier_parents_are_judged`.\n- Format a labelled finding with remedy → `TC-396` expected “with its remedy” → `test_an_entry_names_the_child_the_parent_and_both_statuses`.\n- Make standing cases fail strict integrity and retire the old advisory → `TC-396` expected → `test_an_approved_llr_under_a_drafted_sr_reds_strict_integrity`, `test_the_llr_status_advisory_is_retired`.\n\n**LLR-358**\n\n- Compare changed trees against every parent, including merges → `TC-397` method’s “merge parents” → `test_a_merge_assembling_a_violation_from_two_sides_is_refused`.\n- Report only a relationship whose child or parent status moved → `TC-397` expected → `test_a_commit_moving_neither_row_passes_over_a_standing_case`.\n- Refuse unreadable differences and commit-side unreadable/unparseable registries → `TC-397` expected → `test_a_diff_git_cannot_produce_is_a_refusal_not_a_skip`, `test_a_commit_side_registry_that_cannot_be_read_or_does_not_parse_is_refused_by_name`.\n- Treat parent-side failure as a status movement → `TC-397` expected → `test_a_parent_side_that_does_not_parse_counts_every_status_as_moved`.\n- Treat absent registries as no rows → `TC-397` expected “untouched or absent spine registry” → `test_a_registry_added_with_a_violation_is_refused`, `test_a_commit_repairing_an_unparseable_registry_is_judged_on_its_own_rows`.\n- Leave first commits, untouched registries, and irrelevant status changes unrefused → `TC-397` expected → `test_the_first_commit_is_not_judged`, `test_a_commit_touching_no_registry_is_not_read`.\n- Use the same judgement at staged admission and in the lane walk → `TC-397` expected → `test_the_rule_rides_the_lane_commit_walk`, `test_the_pre_commit_hook_runs_the_parent_first_step`.\n\nGaps: none.\n\nChecks passed:\n\n- `trace.py --strict`: `Traceability: SN=31 SR=137 LLR=325 TC=352 orphans=0 integrity=0 … drafts=5`\n- `check_trajectory.py --strict`: `clean (969 work item(s), 855 done (88%), 34 cancelled, graph acyclic).`\n- Perspective record: `no findings`.\n\nExpected intent-stage advisory: `IF-308` lacks its owner-module `Contract IF-308:` body because the builder creates that body with the call seam. The planned code symbols and tests likewise do not exist yet; neither caused a strict-check failure."}}
